    "guidance": "Validated 4/12 (33.3%); treat as a limited fallback rather than the default. Use only in its documented niche: the state remains within a demonstrated retrieve phase, the path is reachable, and a modest local TCP/qpos mismatch is the main issue; re-evaluate after each 8-action execution chunk. Avoid large peg displacement, uncertain lid-versus-peg phase, and miss/drop/regrasp recovery. All 8 failed runs ended with retrieve_peg_from_box=false and negligible reported peg movement (at most 3.22e-6 m); 5 also ended with the cover closed, while 3 retained an open cover but still did not pick up the peg. Thus no peg rise/co-motion is the clearest observed failure, alongside local-target oscillation/drift or repeated IK failure/limit contact. Handoff to reorient_and_stage_peg only when closed fingers, peg height above the wall, and stable causal peg/TCP co-motion agree; for validated skill completion also require peg center >=0.15 m (or insertion) and cover >0.9 rad. Closure alone is not evidence of grasp."
